This is a joke repository with a little game to be played offline with my friends from university. The game is meant to be accessed via link, and then played in person with a group. What the repository provides is a scoreboard of sorts and the guidelines to play in person, but no game logic has been added.

You can access the game starting your own server and then opening it via browser (useful to prototype and test changes), or via https link thanks to github.

To play released version:
  https://aomartinv.github.io/trivial_2_0/

To develop:

Start server:
  python -m http.server (if unfound later: python -m http.server 8000 --bind 0.0.0.0)
  Open browser and go to http://localhost:8000

To open server from phone:
  Laptop and phone on same wifi
  On laptop, find IP (ipconfig, look for IPv4 address)
  On phone, open browser and go to the address
